window.QUESTION_BANK = (window.QUESTION_BANK || []).concat([
  {"id": "lis_0001", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0001.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Minjun, I've been thinking about our science fair project.\nBoy: The poster? I already picked the colors. Blue and green.\nGirl: That's the thing. I don't think a poster is enough. Everyone does posters.\nBoy: So we start over? It's due Friday.\nGirl: Not start over. Same research. But we show it as a live demonstration, and grow the crystals right in front of the judges.\nBoy: Okay. That would be hard to forget. Let's ask Ms. Park about bringing the equipment.", "stem": "What are the students mainly discussing?", "choices": ["Which colors to use on their poster", "Asking Ms. Park for more time", "Changing the way they will present their project", "Deciding what topic to research"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "포스터 색·마감일·Ms. Park는 모두 언급되지만 곁가지다. 대화의 중심은 '같은 연구를 포스터가 아니라 실연으로 보여주자'는 발표 방식 변경이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "conversation"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0002", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0002.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Ms. Reyes, do you have a minute? It's about band.\nTeacher: Of course. You're thinking of joining?\nBoy: I was. But practice is every Tuesday and Thursday after school. That's when I have math tutoring.\nTeacher: Ah. So the question isn't whether you want to join. It's whether you can.\nBoy: Right. And I don't want to give up tutoring. My grades just came back up.\nTeacher: Then let's not force it this semester. Try the spring auditions instead. Practice moves to mornings then.\nBoy: Mornings I could do.", "stem": "What is the conversation mainly about?", "choices": ["How the student improved his math grades", "How to prepare for the spring auditions", "A scheduling conflict that delays the student's plan", "Why the student wants to stop his tutoring"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "성적·오디션은 언급만 될 뿐이고, '과외를 그만두고 싶어한다'는 선택지는 오히려 반대다(그만두고 싶지 않다고 직접 말한다). 전체를 관통하는 것은 '하고 싶지만 시간이 겹쳐 이번 학기는 미룬다'는 일정 충돌이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "conversation"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0003", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0003.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Did you finish the reading for history?\nBoy: Chapter nine? Yeah. Took me two hours.\nGirl: Two hours! It took me forty minutes.\nBoy: Because you skip the primary sources. I read all the letters and the diary entries.\nGirl: Those aren't on the test.\nBoy: Maybe not. But last week Mr. Cho asked why the farmers moved west, and nobody could answer. It was in the letters.\nGirl: Hm. Okay. Show me how you read them.", "stem": "What is the main point the boy makes?", "choices": ["The extra sources explain things the chapter does not", "The reading assignment is too long for one night", "Mr. Cho asks questions that are unfair", "The girl should spend two hours on homework"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "두 시간·Mr. Cho의 질문은 근거로 든 세부사항이다. 소년의 요지는 '시험에 안 나오는 1차 자료에 교과서가 답하지 못하는 내용이 들어 있다'는 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "conversation"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0004", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0004.m4a", "transcript": "Good morning, students. A note about the library. Starting Monday, the second floor will be closed while new shelves are installed. The first floor stays open, and all the computers have been moved down there. If you have books due that week, don't worry. Nothing counts as late until the second floor reopens on the twentieth. Study rooms can still be booked at the front desk, but there are four now instead of nine, so book early. Thank you.", "stem": "What is the main purpose of the announcement?", "choices": ["To remind students to return overdue books", "To announce that the library will close completely", "To introduce new computers on the first floor", "To explain how library service changes during the work"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "연체·컴퓨터·스터디룸은 모두 '공사 기간 중 이용 방법'의 하위 항목이다. '도서관이 완전히 닫힌다'는 1층은 계속 연다고 했으므로 사실과 다르고, 컴퓨터는 새것이 아니라 1층으로 옮겨진 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "announcement"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0005", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0005.m4a", "transcript": "Attention, seventh graders. You've heard that Field Day is Friday. Yes, it's still happening. But I need to talk about something else. Last year, forty-two water bottles, eleven jackets, and one pair of glasses were left on the field. We kept them a month. Almost nobody came. So this year, each homeroom gets a labeled bin at the edge of the field. Everything goes in your bin, not on the grass. At the end of the day your homeroom teacher carries the bin back inside. Field Day is the fun part. This is the part that decides whether you go home with your things.", "stem": "What is the announcement mainly about?", "choices": ["A new system for keeping track of students' belongings", "How many items students lost last year", "Whether Field Day will take place on Friday", "What homeroom teachers must do on Friday"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Field Day 개최 여부는 첫 문장에서 언급하고 바로 넘어간다('하지만 다른 얘기를 하려고 한다'). 분실물 개수는 근거, 담임 역할은 세부 절차이고, 핵심은 새로 도입하는 물품 관리 방식이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "announcement"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0006", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0006.m4a", "transcript": "So. Octopus arms. Here's what surprised scientists. An octopus has about five hundred million nerve cells, close to a dog. But only a third of them are in its head. The rest are spread through the eight arms. What that means is strange. Each arm can taste, touch, and decide on its own. If an arm is separated from the body, and this has been tested, the arm will still reach for food and pull it toward where the mouth used to be. The octopus doesn't send an order to every arm. It gives a general goal, and the arms work out the details themselves.", "stem": "What is the talk mainly about?", "choices": ["How many nerve cells an octopus has", "How an octopus's arms act largely on their own", "Why octopuses are as intelligent as dogs", "How octopuses find and catch their food"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "신경세포 수와 개 비교는 근거로 든 수치이고, 먹이를 잡는 이야기는 예시다. 전체 요지는 '팔 하나하나가 스스로 판단한다'는 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "academic-talk"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0007", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0007.m4a", "transcript": "When we talk about the invention of paper money, most people picture a government printing bills. That's not how it started. In China, about a thousand years ago, merchants traveling long distances got tired of carrying heavy strings of copper coins. So they left the coins with a trusted shop and took a written receipt instead. The receipt could be traded, and someone in another city would honor it. For almost two hundred years this was a private arrangement between merchants. No emperor involved. The government stepped in only later, once it noticed the paper was already circulating like money. So paper money wasn't handed down from above. It was invented from below, and then taken over.", "stem": "What is the speaker's main point?", "choices": ["Paper money began among merchants before governments took it over", "Copper coins were too heavy to carry on long journeys", "Chinese merchants often traveled between distant cities", "The Chinese government printed the first paper receipts"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "동전의 무거움은 계기, 상인의 이동은 배경 설명이다. '정부가 최초의 지폐를 찍었다'는 정부가 나중에야 개입했다는 내용과 정반대다. 요지는 마지막 문장의 '위에서 내려온 게 아니라 아래에서 발명되어 나중에 접수되었다'이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "academic-talk"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0008", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0008.m4a", "transcript": "Two towns, same river, same year. Town A built a tall concrete wall along the bank. Town B bought the low fields beside the river and let them flood on purpose. They planted grass and put the playground on higher ground. Ten years later, a big storm came. Town A's wall held for six hours, and then the water came around the end of it, into streets that had been built lower and lower because people felt safe. Town B's fields filled up, the water spread out, and the town center stayed dry. Now, the wall wasn't badly built. The problem is what a wall teaches you. It tells you the water will never come, so you stop planning for the day it does.", "stem": "What is the speaker mainly arguing?", "choices": ["Town B was simply luckier than Town A during the storm", "Concrete walls are usually built too weak to hold", "Towns should never be built beside a river", "Flood defenses can create a false sense of safety"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "'the wall wasn't badly built'이라고 직접 부정했으므로 '벽이 부실했다'는 오답이고, 마지막 두 문장이 요지다 — 벽은 '물은 오지 않는다'고 가르쳐서 대비를 멈추게 만든다. '운이 좋았다'가 아니라 구조적 문제를 말하고 있다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "main-idea", "academic-talk"], "replayLimit": 2},
  {"id": "lis_0009", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0009.m4a", "transcript": "I didn't say she took the book.", "transcriptMarked": "I didn't say **SHE** took the book.  ← 'she'에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker most likely mean?", "choices": ["She may have taken something other than the book", "Someone other than her may have taken the book", "The speaker never mentioned the book at all", "She borrowed the book rather than took it"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "글자는 같아도 강세 위치가 뜻을 정한다. 'she'를 강조하면 '그 애가 가져갔다고는 안 했다' = 다른 사람일 수 있다는 뜻. 'book'을 강조했다면 '책이 아닌 다른 것을 가져갔다'가 답이 된다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0010", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0010.m4a", "transcript": "I asked for the blue folder on my desk.", "transcriptMarked": "I asked for the blue folder on **MY** desk.  ← 'my'에 강세", "stem": "What mistake is the speaker correcting?", "choices": ["The wrong color folder was brought", "The folder was taken from someone else's desk", "The folder was not on a desk at all", "More than one folder was brought"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'my'에 강세가 놓였으므로 대조되는 것은 '내 책상 vs 다른 사람 책상'이다. 색깔이 문제였다면 'blue'에 강세가 왔을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0011", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0011.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: They moved practice to six in the morning.\nGirl: Oh, that's just great.", "transcriptMarked": "Oh, that's just great.  ← 평탄하고 느린 내림조 = 비꼼", "stem": "How does the girl feel about the change?", "choices": ["She is pleased that practice will be earlier", "She is unhappy about the new time", "She is surprised no one told her sooner", "She thinks the new time is fair to everyone"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "단어만 보면 칭찬이지만 어조가 반대를 말한다. 느리고 낮게 깔리는 평탄한 억양은 영어에서 전형적인 비꼼(sarcasm) 신호다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0012", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0012.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Good news. I've put you in the front row for the concert.\nBoy: Thank you. That's very kind.", "transcriptMarked": "Thank you. ⟨0.6초 휴지⟩ That's very kind.  ← 예의는 갖추되 가라앉은 어조", "stem": "What does the boy's tone suggest?", "choices": ["He did not hear which concert she meant", "He is less pleased than his words suggest", "He is genuinely delighted with the seat", "He is confused about where to sit"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'감사합니다'라는 말과 달리 휴지와 가라앉은 억양이 반가움 없음을 드러낸다. 말의 내용과 어조가 어긋날 때는 어조 쪽이 진심이다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0013", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0013.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Can you have the report ready by tomorrow?\nGirl: Well, I suppose I could try.", "transcriptMarked": "Well, ⟨0.5초⟩ I suppose ⟨0.32초⟩ I could try.  ← 휴지 + 느린 속도", "stem": "How does the girl feel about the deadline?", "choices": ["She is reluctant and not at all sure", "She is confident she will finish in time", "She has already finished the report", "She did not understand the question"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'할 수 있다'가 아니라 '해 볼 수는 있을 것 같다'에 긴 휴지가 겹쳤다. 휴지와 채움말(well)은 내키지 않음·자신 없음의 신호다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0014", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0014.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Did you like my painting? Be honest.\nBoy: It's really... interesting.", "transcriptMarked": "⟨0.9초 침묵⟩ It's really... interesting.  ← 답 앞의 긴 침묵", "stem": "What does the boy's pause suggest?", "choices": ["He did not hear her question clearly", "He is genuinely impressed by the painting", "He wants her to ask the question again", "He is looking for a polite way to avoid criticizing it"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "칭찬이 진심이면 즉시 나온다. 대답 앞의 긴 침묵과 'interesting' 앞의 머뭇거림은 부정적인 평가를 돌려 말하려는 신호다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0015", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0015.m4a", "transcript": "You finished the whole thing?", "transcriptMarked": "You finished the whole thing↗  ← 문장 끝이 올라감", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Expressing surprise and checking if it is true", "Giving the listener an instruction", "Complaining that the work took too long", "Stating a fact she already knew"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "어순은 평서문이지만 끝을 올려 읽으면 놀람 섞인 확인 질문이 된다. 내려 읽었다면 이미 알고 있는 사실을 담담히 말하는 진술이 된다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0016", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0016.m4a", "transcript": "For the project you'll need paper, scissors, glue...", "transcriptMarked": "paper↗, scissors↗, glue↗  ← 마지막 항목도 올림조 = 목록 계속됨", "stem": "What does the speaker's intonation tell you?", "choices": ["These three items are the only ones needed", "The speaker is unsure the items are necessary", "The list is not finished yet", "The speaker is asking someone to bring the items"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "영어 목록에서 마지막 항목은 내림조로 끝나 완결을 알린다. 여기서는 'glue'까지 올림조라 항목이 더 남았다는 신호.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0017", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0017.m4a", "transcript": "We're meeting at the library on Thursday.", "transcriptMarked": "We're meeting at the library on **THURSDAY**.  ← 요일에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker correcting?", "choices": ["The place of the meeting", "The day of the meeting", "Who is coming to the meeting", "The time the meeting starts"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'Thursday'에 강세가 있으므로 대조되는 것은 '다른 요일'이다. 장소를 바로잡는 것이었다면 'library'에 강세가 왔을 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0018", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0018.m4a", "transcript": "We're meeting at the library on Thursday.", "transcriptMarked": "We're meeting at the **LIBRARY** on Thursday.  ← 장소에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker correcting?", "choices": ["The day of the meeting", "Who is coming to the meeting", "Whether the meeting will happen", "The place of the meeting"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "앞 문항과 글자는 똑같지만 강세가 'library'로 옮겨졌다. 따라서 바로잡는 것은 장소이고, 요일은 문제가 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0019", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0019.m4a", "transcript": "Jenny brought the cookies to the party.", "transcriptMarked": "**JENNY** brought the cookies to the party.  ← 사람 이름에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker's stress suggest?", "choices": ["Jenny brought something other than cookies", "Someone thought a different person brought them", "Jenny took the cookies somewhere else", "Jenny did not go to the party"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "주어에 강세가 놓이면 '다른 사람이 아니라 바로 그 사람'이라는 대조가 된다. 가져온 물건을 바로잡는 것이었다면 'cookies'에 강세가 왔을 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0020", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0020.m4a", "transcript": "Jenny brought the cookies to the party.", "transcriptMarked": "Jenny brought the **COOKIES** to the party.  ← 물건에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker's stress suggest?", "choices": ["A different person brought the cookies", "Jenny arrived late to the party", "The party was held somewhere else", "Jenny was expected to bring something else"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "목적어에 강세가 오면 '다른 것이 아니라 이것'이라는 뜻이다. 사람을 바로잡는 것이었다면 'Jenny'에 강세가 왔을 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0021", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0021.m4a", "transcript": "I never said the test was easy.", "transcriptMarked": "I never said the test was **EASY**.  ← 'easy'에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker mean?", "choices": ["He said something else about the test", "Someone else called the test easy", "He never mentioned the test at all", "He was talking about a different test"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'easy'에 강세가 있으므로 시험 얘기는 했지만 '쉽다'고는 안 했다는 뜻이다. 'I'에 강세였다면 '다른 사람이 그렇게 말했다', 'said'에 강세였다면 '생각은 했지만 입 밖에 내진 않았다'가 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0022", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0022.m4a", "transcript": "I never said the test was easy.", "transcriptMarked": "**I** never said the test was easy.  ← 'I'에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker mean?", "choices": ["He said something else about the test", "He thought it but did not say it", "Someone else said that, not him", "He does not remember the test"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "주어에 강세가 오면 '내가 아니라 다른 사람'이라는 대조다. 같은 문장이라도 강세가 'easy'에 있었다면 뜻이 완전히 달라진다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0023", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0023.m4a", "transcript": "He told me to wait here.", "transcriptMarked": "He told me to wait **HERE**.  ← 장소 부사에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker emphasizing?", "choices": ["Who gave him the instruction", "The exact place he was told to wait", "How long he has to wait", "That he was told, not asked"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "장소를 나타내는 'here'에 강세가 있으므로 '다른 데가 아니라 바로 여기'라는 뜻이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0024", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0024.m4a", "transcript": "The homework is due tomorrow.", "transcriptMarked": "The homework is due **TOMORROW**.  ← 기한에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker's stress suggest?", "choices": ["A different assignment is due", "Someone was wrong about the deadline", "The homework is optional", "The homework was already collected"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "기한을 나타내는 단어에 강세가 놓이면 대개 상대가 잘못 알고 있는 날짜를 바로잡는 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0025", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0025.m4a", "transcript": "My sister borrowed my jacket.", "transcriptMarked": "My sister borrowed **MY** jacket.  ← 소유격에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker pointing out?", "choices": ["Her sister took it without asking", "Her sister borrowed it, not bought it", "Her sister took a jacket, not a coat", "It was her jacket, not someone else's"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "소유격에 강세가 오면 '누구의 것인가'가 초점이다. 빌린 행위 자체가 초점이었다면 'borrowed'에 강세가 왔을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0026", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0026.m4a", "transcript": "My sister borrowed my jacket.", "transcriptMarked": "My sister **BORROWED** my jacket.  ← 동사에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker pointing out?", "choices": ["It was hers, not her sister's", "Her sister, not someone else, took it", "The jacket was new", "It will be returned - it was not taken for good"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "동사에 강세가 오면 행위의 성격이 초점이다. 'borrow(빌리다)'를 강조하면 '가져가 버린 게 아니라 빌린 것'이라는 뜻이 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0027", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0027.m4a", "transcript": "We walked to school this morning.", "transcriptMarked": "We **WALKED** to school this morning.  ← 동사에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker mean?", "choices": ["They went to school, not somewhere else", "They went this morning, not yesterday", "They went on foot rather than by bus or car", "Only some of them went to school"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "이동 방법을 나타내는 동사에 강세가 놓였으므로 '다른 수단이 아니라 걸어서'라는 대조가 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0028", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0028.m4a", "transcript": "I put your lunch in the fridge.", "transcriptMarked": "I put your lunch in the **FRIDGE**.  ← 장소에 강세", "stem": "Why does the speaker stress that word?", "choices": ["To say whose lunch it is", "To say what the food is", "To say who put it there", "To say where to find it"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "장소 명사에 강세가 있으면 '어디에 있는지'가 핵심 정보다. 아마 상대가 다른 곳을 찾고 있었을 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0029", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0029.m4a", "transcript": "She's not coming to the concert tonight.", "transcriptMarked": "She's not coming to the concert **TONIGHT**.  ← 시점에 강세", "stem": "What can be understood from the stress?", "choices": ["She dislikes concerts in general", "Someone else is coming instead", "The concert has been canceled", "She may come to a different concert another time"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "부정문에서 시점에 강세가 오면 부정의 범위가 그 시점으로 좁혀진다. 즉 '오늘 밤은 안 오지만 다른 때는 올 수도'라는 뜻이 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0030", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0030.m4a", "transcript": "We can't leave until everyone is ready.", "transcriptMarked": "We can't leave until **EVERYONE** is ready.  ← 'everyone'에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker emphasizing?", "choices": ["They will leave very soon", "No one may be left behind", "They cannot leave at all today", "Being ready is not important"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'everyone'에 강세를 주면 '한 사람도 빠짐없이'라는 뜻이 강조된다. 대부분이 준비된 것으로는 부족하다는 의미.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0031", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0031.m4a", "transcript": "They finished the project without any help.", "transcriptMarked": "They finished the project without **ANY** help.  ← 'any'에 강세", "stem": "What does the stress add to the sentence?", "choices": ["That the project was difficult", "That they wanted help but got none", "That they had absolutely no help at all", "That the project is not finished yet"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "부정어와 함께 쓰인 'any'에 강세를 주면 '조금도 없었다'는 완전 부정이 강조된다. 놀라움이나 감탄이 담긴다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0032", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0032.m4a", "transcript": "That's not what I meant.", "transcriptMarked": "That's not what **I** meant.  ← 'I'에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker suggesting?", "choices": ["She does not understand the question", "She changed her mind about it", "Someone else may have meant that, but she did not", "She agrees with what was said"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'I'에 강세를 주면 '내 뜻은 그게 아니다 — 그렇게 말한 건 다른 사람'이라는 대조가 생긴다. 'meant'에 강세였다면 단순히 '오해했다'는 뜻에 그친다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0033", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0033.m4a", "transcript": "You should have told me earlier.", "transcriptMarked": "You should have told me **EARLIER**.  ← 시점 부사에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker's point?", "choices": ["He was told by the wrong person", "He was never told at all", "The problem was the timing, not the telling", "He does not want to hear about it"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'earlier'에 강세가 오므로 말한 것 자체는 문제가 아니고 '더 일찍 했어야 했다'는 시점이 초점이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0034", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0034.m4a", "transcript": "The teacher gave us three examples.", "transcriptMarked": "The teacher gave us **THREE** examples.  ← 숫자에 강세", "stem": "Why is that word stressed?", "choices": ["Because the number is being corrected", "Because the examples were difficult", "Because a different teacher gave them", "Because the examples were not helpful"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "숫자에 강세가 놓이면 대개 상대가 잘못 기억한 개수를 바로잡는 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0035", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0035.m4a", "transcript": "I can hear the music from my room.", "transcriptMarked": "I can **HEAR** the music from my room.  ← 지각동사에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker most likely mean?", "choices": ["The music is coming from another room", "He wants the music turned up", "He can hear it even if he cannot see it", "He is listening in his own room"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "감각을 나타내는 동사에 강세가 오면 다른 감각과의 대조가 생긴다. 여기서는 '보이지는 않아도 들린다'는 뜻.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0036", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0036.m4a", "transcript": "I borrowed the book from the library.", "transcriptMarked": "I **BORROWED** the book from the library.  ← 동사에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker making clear?", "choices": ["She went to the library, not a bookstore", "She did not buy or keep the book", "She took a book, not a magazine", "She went there by herself"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "동사에 강세를 주어 행위의 성격을 분명히 한다 — 사거나 가진 게 아니라 빌린 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0037", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0037.m4a", "transcript": "She wants to study science in college.", "transcriptMarked": "She wants to study **SCIENCE** in college.  ← 과목에 강세", "stem": "What does the stress tell you?", "choices": ["She is not sure about her plan", "The subject is what matters here", "She will study somewhere far away", "She has already started studying"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "과목 이름에 강세가 놓였으므로 '다른 전공이 아니라 과학'이라는 점이 초점이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0038", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0038.m4a", "transcript": "He said the answer was on page ten.", "transcriptMarked": "He said the answer was on page **TEN**.  ← 쪽수에 강세", "stem": "What is being corrected?", "choices": ["Which page number it is", "Who gave the information", "Whether there is an answer", "Which book to look in"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "쪽수에 강세가 있으므로 다른 쪽을 보고 있는 상대를 바로잡는 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0039", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0039.m4a", "transcript": "My brother doesn't like spicy food.", "transcriptMarked": "My **BROTHER** doesn't like spicy food.  ← 주어에 강세", "stem": "What can be understood from the stress?", "choices": ["Her brother dislikes all food", "Her brother has never tried spicy food", "Other people in the family do like it", "She does not like spicy food either"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "부정문의 주어에 강세를 주면 '그 사람만 그렇다'는 대조가 생겨, 나머지는 반대라는 뜻이 함께 전달된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0040", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0040.m4a", "transcript": "The meeting starts at two thirty.", "transcriptMarked": "The meeting starts at two **THIRTY**.  ← 분에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker correcting?", "choices": ["The minutes past the hour", "The hour of the meeting", "The day of the meeting", "Where the meeting is held"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'two'가 아니라 'thirty'에 강세가 있으므로 시(hour)가 아니라 분을 바로잡는 것이다. 아마 상대가 2시로 알고 있었을 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0041", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0041.m4a", "transcript": "I already told her about the change.", "transcriptMarked": "I **ALREADY** told her about the change.  ← 'already'에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker mean?", "choices": ["He told the wrong person", "He will tell her soon", "There is no need to tell her again", "He forgot to tell her"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'already'를 강조하면 '이미 끝난 일이니 또 할 필요 없다'는 뜻이 된다. 살짝 답답함이 묻어나기도 한다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0042", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0042.m4a", "transcript": "You can borrow mine if you need one.", "transcriptMarked": "You can borrow **MINE** if you need one.  ← 소유대명사에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker emphasizing?", "choices": ["That she needs one too", "That borrowing is not allowed", "That she is offering her own", "That she will buy a new one"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "소유대명사에 강세를 주면 '남의 것이 아니라 내 것'을 빌려주겠다는 제안이 분명해진다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0043", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0043.m4a", "transcript": "I only had one question about your essay.", "transcriptMarked": "I only had **ONE** question about your essay.  ← 수량에 강세", "stem": "What is the speaker suggesting?", "choices": ["The essay had many problems", "She had just a single small concern", "She did not read the essay", "She wants the essay rewritten"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'only'와 함께 숫자에 강세를 주면 '그만큼 적다'가 강조된다. 즉 대체로 잘 썼다는 긍정적 신호에 가깝다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0044", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0044.m4a", "transcript": "I thought you were going to call me.", "transcriptMarked": "I thought **YOU** were going to call me.  ← 'you'에 강세", "stem": "What does the speaker mean?", "choices": ["He forgot to make the call himself", "He expected the other person to call", "He does not have the phone number", "He called but no one answered"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'you'에 강세가 오면 '전화할 사람은 내가 아니라 너였다'는 책임 소재의 대조가 된다. 가벼운 항의가 담긴다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "stress"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0067", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0067.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: The bus leaves at five in the morning.\nGirl: Perfect.", "transcriptMarked": "Perfect.  ← 느리고 낮은 평탄한 어조 = 비꼼", "stem": "How does the girl feel about the departure time?", "choices": ["She thinks it is a good time", "She is not happy about it", "She did not hear the time", "She wants to leave even earlier"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'Perfect'는 칭찬하는 말이지만, 느리게 끌며 낮게 깔면 정반대를 뜻한다. 말과 어조가 어긋날 때는 어조가 진심이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0068", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0068.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: We have another test on Monday.\nGirl: Wonderful.", "transcriptMarked": "Wonderful.  ← 가라앉은 평탄한 어조 = 비꼼", "stem": "What does the girl actually mean?", "choices": ["She is looking forward to the test", "She has already finished studying", "She thinks the test was canceled", "She is dreading the test"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "긍정적인 단어를 무표정하게 말하면 반어가 된다. 진심이었다면 밝고 빠르게 올라가는 억양이었을 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0069", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0069.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: I fixed the printer. It only took two hours.\nBoy: Nice work.", "transcriptMarked": "Nice work.  ← 밝고 따뜻한 어조 = 진심", "stem": "How does the boy mean his comment?", "choices": ["As a genuine compliment", "As a complaint about the printer", "As a sarcastic remark", "As a request for help"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "같은 칭찬이라도 밝고 활기찬 어조면 진심이다. 비꼼이었다면 느리고 평탄하게 말했을 것 — 어조로만 구분된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0070", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0070.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: I finished the whole poster by myself.\nBoy: Nice work.", "transcriptMarked": "Nice work.  ← 느리고 낮은 어조 = 진심 아님", "stem": "How does the boy mean his comment?", "choices": ["He is genuinely impressed", "He wants to help with the poster", "He did not see the poster", "He is not being sincere"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "앞 문항과 대사가 완전히 같지만 어조가 반대다. 소리를 듣지 않으면 절대 구분할 수 없는 문항이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0071", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0071.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: I moved your presentation to first period.\nBoy: Oh. Okay, sure.", "transcriptMarked": "Oh. ⟨0.5초⟩ Okay, sure.  ← 'Oh' 뒤의 멈칫 + 가라앉은 어조", "stem": "What does the boy's tone show?", "choices": ["He accepts it but is not pleased", "He is glad to go first", "He does not understand the change", "He refuses to present"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Okay, sure'는 수락이지만 앞의 'Oh'와 짧은 멈칫, 그리고 힘 빠진 어조가 내키지 않음을 드러낸다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0072", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0072.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Would you like to lead the group project?\nGirl: Yes! I'd love to.", "transcriptMarked": "Yes! I'd love to.  ← 빠르고 높은 어조 = 진심 어린 열의", "stem": "How does the girl feel?", "choices": ["Worried about the work", "Unsure whether she can", "Eager to take the role", "Annoyed at being asked"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "망설임 없이 빠르고 밝게 대답하면 진짜 하고 싶다는 뜻이다. 같은 말도 느리게 하면 마지못한 수락이 된다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0073", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0073.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Would you like to lead the group project?\nGirl: Yes. I'd love to.", "transcriptMarked": "Yes. ⟨0.7초⟩ I'd love to.  ← 대답 뒤 긴 멈춤 + 느린 속도", "stem": "How does the girl feel?", "choices": ["Genuinely excited about it", "Confused about the project", "Angry at the teacher", "Willing but clearly reluctant"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "말은 앞 문항과 똑같지만 중간의 긴 휴지와 느린 속도가 진심이 아님을 알려 준다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0074", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0074.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Did we win?\nGirl: We came in second.", "transcriptMarked": "We came in second.  ← 가라앉은 어조 = 실망", "stem": "How does the girl feel about the result?", "choices": ["Proud of second place", "Surprised they placed at all", "Disappointed by the result", "Unsure of the final score"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "2등은 좋은 성적일 수도 있지만, 힘없이 내려가는 어조는 기대에 못 미쳤다는 뜻이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0075", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0075.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Did we win?\nGirl: We came in second!", "transcriptMarked": "We came in second!  ← 밝고 높은 어조 = 기쁨", "stem": "How does the girl feel about the result?", "choices": ["Embarrassed by the result", "Indifferent to the result", "Confused about the scoring", "Delighted with the result"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "같은 사실도 어조에 따라 평가가 달라진다. 밝게 올라가는 억양이면 기대 이상의 좋은 결과였다는 뜻.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0076", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0076.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Good news. The field trip is back on.\nBoy: Oh, thank goodness.", "transcriptMarked": "Oh, thank goodness.  ← 한숨 섞인 편안한 어조 = 안도", "stem": "How does the boy feel?", "choices": ["Annoyed", "Relieved", "Confused", "Uninterested"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "긴장이 풀리는 어조로 말하는 'thank goodness'는 걱정하던 일이 해결됐을 때의 안도를 나타낸다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0077", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0077.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: The science club meets at lunch now.\nBoy: Since when?", "transcriptMarked": "Since when?  ← 날 선 어조 = 의심 섞인 불만", "stem": "What does the boy's tone suggest?", "choices": ["He is happy about the new time", "He is asking for directions", "He has already been attending", "He is doubtful and a little put out"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "'Since when?'을 퉁명스럽게 말하면 단순한 질문이 아니라 '그런 얘기 못 들었는데'라는 불만이 담긴다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0078", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0078.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Do you think my drawing is good enough for the contest?\nGirl: It's definitely... unusual.", "transcriptMarked": "⟨0.9초 침묵⟩ It's definitely... unusual.  ← 대답 전 긴 침묵 + 단어 고르기", "stem": "What does the girl's pause suggest?", "choices": ["She is genuinely impressed", "She did not hear the question", "She is avoiding an honest criticism", "She wants to enter the contest too"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "칭찬이 진심이면 바로 나온다. 긴 침묵과 'unusual' 앞의 머뭇거림은 부정적 평가를 돌려 말하려는 신호다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0079", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0079.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: You'll need to redo the second half.\nGirl: All of it?", "transcriptMarked": "All of it?  ← 힘 빠진 어조 = 낙담", "stem": "How does the girl feel?", "choices": ["Pleased to have another chance", "Certain the teacher is wrong", "Discouraged by the amount of work", "Eager to begin again"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "같은 질문도 밝게 물으면 확인이지만, 가라앉은 어조로 물으면 '그렇게까지?' 하는 낙담이 담긴다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0080", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0080.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: I studied for six hours yesterday.\nBoy: Six hours.", "transcriptMarked": "Six hours.  ← 느리게 되뇌는 평탄한 어조 = 의심", "stem": "What does the boy's tone show?", "choices": ["He believes her completely", "He is impressed by her effort", "He studied even longer", "He doubts what she is saying"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "상대의 말을 느리게 되풀이하며 평탄하게 말하면 '정말?' 하는 의심이 담긴다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0081", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0081.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Your grade went up ten points this term.\nBoy: Really? That's great!", "transcriptMarked": "Really? That's great!  ← 빠르고 높은 어조 = 진짜 기쁨", "stem": "How does the boy feel?", "choices": ["Genuinely pleased and a bit surprised", "Suspicious of the teacher", "Disappointed with the increase", "Uninterested in his grade"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "빠르고 높은 억양은 꾸밈없는 기쁨이다. 같은 말이라도 느리고 평탄하면 비꼼이 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0082", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0082.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Can you help me carry these boxes?\nGirl: I guess so.", "transcriptMarked": "I guess so.  ← 느리고 낮게 = 마지못한 승낙", "stem": "How willing is the girl to help?", "choices": ["Willing but without enthusiasm", "Very willing", "Completely unwilling", "Unable to hear the request"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'I guess so'는 그 자체로도 소극적인 표현인데, 느리고 낮은 어조까지 겹치면 마지못해 응하는 것이 분명해진다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0083", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0083.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Can you help me carry these boxes?\nGirl: Sure, no problem!", "transcriptMarked": "Sure, no problem!  ← 밝고 따뜻한 어조 = 흔쾌한 승낙", "stem": "How willing is the girl to help?", "choices": ["Helping only out of duty", "Refusing politely", "Asking for something in return", "Happy to help"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "밝고 빠른 어조는 기꺼이 돕겠다는 뜻이다. 앞 문항과 비교하면 어조의 차이가 분명하게 들린다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0084", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0084.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: The results come out tomorrow.\nGirl: Tomorrow.", "transcriptMarked": "Tomorrow.  ← 떨리고 조심스러운 어조 = 긴장", "stem": "How does the girl feel?", "choices": ["Nervous about the results", "Excited to see the results", "Certain she did well", "Unaware of the test"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "단어 하나를 조심스럽게 되뇌는 것은 그 일이 부담스럽다는 뜻이다. 기대였다면 밝게 올라갔을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0085", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0085.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: I rewrote the ending three times.\nTeacher: I can tell.", "transcriptMarked": "I can tell.  ← 따뜻하게 올라가는 어조 = 긍정적 인정", "stem": "What does the teacher mean?", "choices": ["The writing looks careless", "She wants it rewritten again", "The effort shows in a good way", "She did not read the ending"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'I can tell'은 어조에 따라 칭찬도 지적도 된다. 밝고 따뜻하면 '노력이 보인다'는 칭찬이다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0086", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0086.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: I wrote it during lunch break.\nTeacher: I can tell.", "transcriptMarked": "I can tell.  ← 느리고 냉랭한 어조 = 지적", "stem": "What does the teacher mean?", "choices": ["The rushed work is obvious", "She is impressed by the speed", "She wants to hear more about it", "She did not receive the work"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "앞 문항과 똑같은 말이지만 차갑고 느린 어조다. '급하게 쓴 티가 난다'는 부정적 평가가 된다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0087", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0087.m4a", "transcript": "Announcer: Practice is canceled due to rain.\nBoy: Again?", "transcriptMarked": "Again?  ← 날카롭게 튀어 오르는 어조 = 짜증", "stem": "How does the boy feel?", "choices": ["Frustrated that it keeps happening", "Relieved to have a free afternoon", "Confused about the schedule", "Glad the weather is bad"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Again?'을 날카롭게 말하면 반복되는 상황에 대한 짜증이다. 안도였다면 부드럽게 내려갔을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0088", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0088.m4a", "transcript": "Announcer: The math quiz has been postponed to Friday.\nGirl: Oh, good.", "transcriptMarked": "Oh, good.  ← 긴장이 풀리는 부드러운 어조 = 안도", "stem": "How does the girl feel?", "choices": ["Relieved to have more time", "Upset about the delay", "Doubtful that it is true", "Indifferent to the change"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "숨을 내쉬듯 부드럽게 말하는 'Oh, good'은 걱정거리가 미뤄져 마음이 놓였다는 뜻이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0089", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0089.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Can anyone explain the second step?\nBoy: I think... maybe it's the temperature?", "transcriptMarked": "I think... maybe it's the temperature↗  ← 머뭇거림 + 끝을 올림", "stem": "How confident is the boy?", "choices": ["Completely sure of his answer", "Sure but unwilling to say", "Not at all sure", "He is joking"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'I think', 'maybe'에 머뭇거림과 올라가는 끝이 겹치면 자신 없음이 분명하다. 확신이 있으면 끝을 내려 단정한다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0090", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0090.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Can anyone explain the second step?\nBoy: It's the temperature.", "transcriptMarked": "It's the temperature↘  ← 망설임 없이 내려 끝맺음", "stem": "How confident is the boy?", "choices": ["Clearly confident", "Uncertain and guessing", "Reluctant to answer", "Asking rather than answering"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "머뭇거림 없이 끝을 내려 단정하면 확신이 있다는 뜻이다. 앞 문항과 정보는 같지만 태도가 정반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0091", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0091.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: So we're meeting at my house on Saturday?\nGirl: That works. I think.", "transcriptMarked": "That works. ⟨0.6초⟩ I think.  ← 동의 뒤 덧붙인 유보", "stem": "What does the girl's delivery suggest?", "choices": ["The plan is firmly settled", "She has a doubt she is not stating", "She cannot come at all", "She wants to meet somewhere else"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "먼저 동의해 놓고 잠시 뒤 'I think'를 덧붙이면 확신이 흔들린다는 신호다. 말하지 않은 걸림돌이 있을 수 있다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0092", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0092.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: I've read your report.\nGirl: And?", "transcriptMarked": "And?  ← 조심스럽고 작은 목소리 = 불안", "stem": "How does the girl feel?", "choices": ["Impatient and rude", "Bored by the topic", "Anxious about the response", "Proud of her report"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "짧은 'And?'도 조심스럽고 떨리는 어조면 결과를 두려워하는 것이다. 퉁명스러웠다면 무례함이 됐을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0093", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0093.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: My little brother drew on my homework.\nBoy: That's rough.", "transcriptMarked": "That's rough.  ← 부드럽고 따뜻한 어조 = 공감", "stem": "What is the boy doing?", "choices": ["Making fun of her", "Blaming her for it", "Sympathizing with her", "Changing the subject"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "부드럽게 내려가는 공감의 어조다. 같은 말을 밝고 가볍게 던졌다면 놀리는 것으로 들렸을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0094", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0094.m4a", "transcript": "Everyone, please put your phones away.", "transcriptMarked": "put your phones away↘  ← 단호하게 내려 끝맺음", "stem": "What is the teacher's tone?", "choices": ["Gentle and joking", "Sad and disappointed", "Firm and slightly impatient", "Uncertain and questioning"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'please'가 붙어 있어도 단호하게 내려 끝맺으면 부탁이 아니라 지시다. 이미 한 번 말했을 가능성이 크다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0095", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0095.m4a", "transcript": "Everyone, please put your phones away.", "transcriptMarked": "put your phones away  ← 부드럽고 밝은 어조", "stem": "What is the teacher's tone?", "choices": ["Angry and scolding", "Worried and rushed", "Pleasant and routine", "Sarcastic and cold"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "같은 문장이라도 부드러운 어조면 늘 하는 안내에 가깝다. 앞 문항과 비교해 들으면 차이가 분명하다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0096", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0096.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: I'll have the slides ready by tonight.\nGirl: You will.", "transcriptMarked": "You will.  ← 느리고 평탄하게 되받음 = 못 믿겠다는 뜻", "stem": "What is the girl expressing?", "choices": ["Doubt that he will do it", "Confidence in his promise", "A request for the slides", "Praise for his planning"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "상대의 말을 그대로 되받으며 평탄하게 내려 말하면 '과연 그럴까'라는 의심이 된다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0097", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0097.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: You're welcome to join the trip, but the fee is due Friday.\nGirl: Friday.", "transcriptMarked": "Friday.  ← 가라앉게 되뇜 = 곤란함", "stem": "What does the girl's tone suggest?", "choices": ["She is glad it is so soon", "She has already paid the fee", "She does not want to go", "The date may be a problem for her"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "날짜를 무겁게 되뇌는 것은 그 조건이 부담스럽다는 신호다. 가고 싶지 않다면 관심 자체를 보이지 않았을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0098", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0098.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Was the movie any good?\nBoy: It was... fine.", "transcriptMarked": "It was... fine.  ← 'fine' 앞의 머뭇거림", "stem": "What does the boy think of the movie?", "choices": ["He loved it", "He did not see it", "He thought it was disappointing", "He fell asleep during it"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'fine'은 긍정어지만 앞에서 머뭇거리면 '그저 그랬다'는 완곡한 부정이 된다. 좋았다면 바로 대답했을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0099", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0099.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Was the movie any good?\nBoy: It was great!", "transcriptMarked": "It was great!  ← 즉각적이고 밝은 대답", "stem": "What does the boy think of the movie?", "choices": ["He is being polite about a bad film", "He is unsure what he thought", "He has not seen it yet", "He really enjoyed it"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "망설임 없이 밝게 대답하면 진심이다. 앞 문항의 머뭇거리는 'fine'과 나란히 들어 보면 차이가 뚜렷하다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0100", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0100.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: I noticed you've been quiet in class lately.\nBoy: I'm fine.", "transcriptMarked": "I'm fine.  ← 힘없이 내려가는 어조", "stem": "What does the boy's tone suggest?", "choices": ["He is genuinely doing well", "Something may be bothering him", "He did not hear the teacher", "He is annoyed by the question"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'I'm fine'을 힘없이 말하면 대개 괜찮지 않다는 뜻이다. 말의 내용보다 어조가 진실에 가깝다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0101", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0101.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Sorry, I forgot to bring your book again.\nGirl: It's okay.", "transcriptMarked": "It's okay.  ← 짧고 차갑게 = 괜찮지 않음", "stem": "What does the girl actually feel?", "choices": ["She truly does not mind", "She never lent him a book", "She wants him to keep it", "She is bothered but says otherwise"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "'It's okay'를 차갑고 짧게 말하면 실제로는 서운하다는 뜻이다. 진심이면 부드럽고 따뜻하게 말한다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0102", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0102.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Sorry, I forgot to bring your book again.\nGirl: It's okay!", "transcriptMarked": "It's okay!  ← 밝고 따뜻하게 = 진심", "stem": "What does the girl actually feel?", "choices": ["She is hiding her annoyance", "She is confused by the apology", "She wants the book back today", "She genuinely does not mind"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "같은 말이라도 밝고 따뜻하면 진짜 괜찮다는 뜻이다. 어조 하나로 정반대가 되는 표현이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0103", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0103.m4a", "transcript": "Announcer: Attention. The gym will be closed all week.\nBoy: All week.", "transcriptMarked": "All week.  ← 느리고 무겁게 되뇜 = 낙담", "stem": "How does the boy react?", "choices": ["He is dismayed by how long it is", "He is pleased by the news", "He did not understand the notice", "He rarely uses the gym"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "기간을 무겁게 되뇌는 것은 그 길이가 뜻밖이고 달갑지 않다는 뜻이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0104", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0104.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: Your teammate says you did most of the work.\nGirl: We both worked on it.", "transcriptMarked": "We both worked on it.  ← 부드럽고 담담한 어조 = 겸양", "stem": "What is the girl doing?", "choices": ["Complaining about her teammate", "Modestly sharing the credit", "Denying that she helped", "Asking for a better grade"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "따뜻하고 담담한 어조로 공을 나누면 겸손한 태도다. 불만이었다면 힘주어 날카롭게 말했을 것.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0105", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0105.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Are you coming to my recital?\nBoy: I'll try to make it.", "transcriptMarked": "I'll try to make it.  ← 느리고 낮게 = 확답 회피", "stem": "How likely is the boy to come?", "choices": ["He has definitely decided to come", "He has already bought a ticket", "He is not really committing", "He refuses to come"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "'try'라는 단어 자체가 여지를 남기는데, 느리고 낮은 어조까지 겹치면 사실상 확답을 피하는 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0106", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0106.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: Are you coming to my recital?\nBoy: I wouldn't miss it!", "transcriptMarked": "I wouldn't miss it!  ← 힘 있고 밝은 어조 = 확실한 약속", "stem": "How likely is the boy to come?", "choices": ["He is politely refusing", "He is definitely coming", "He has not decided", "He forgot about the recital"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "망설임 없는 밝은 어조는 확실한 약속이다. 앞 문항의 'I'll try'와 나란히 들어 보면 온도 차가 분명하다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0107", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0107.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: I think we should start over.\nGirl: We could do that.", "transcriptMarked": "We could do that.  ← 느리고 낮은 어조 = 완곡한 반대", "stem": "What is the girl really saying?", "choices": ["She fully agrees with the idea", "She would rather not, but is being polite", "She has already started over", "She does not understand the plan"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "'could'로 여지만 남기고 어조까지 가라앉으면 사실상 반대다. 찬성이었다면 'Yes, let's!'처럼 밝게 답했을 것.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0108", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0108.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: You've improved a lot since September.\nBoy: Thanks!", "transcriptMarked": "You've improved a lot!  /  Thanks!  ← 양쪽 다 밝고 빠른 어조", "stem": "What is the mood of this exchange?", "choices": ["Tense and formal", "Cold and distant", "Confused and unclear", "Warm and encouraging"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "두 사람 모두 밝고 빠른 어조로 주고받으면 따뜻하고 격려하는 분위기다. 어조가 대화 전체의 온도를 정한다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "attitude"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0045", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0045.m4a", "transcript": "You're coming with us?", "transcriptMarked": "You're coming with us↗  ← 끝을 올림 = 확인 질문", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Telling the listener what to do", "Checking something she is unsure about", "Refusing to go along", "Complaining about the plan"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "어순은 평서문이지만 끝을 올리면 질문이 된다. 내려 읽었다면 '너도 같이 가는 거야'라는 통보가 된다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0046", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0046.m4a", "transcript": "You're coming with us.", "transcriptMarked": "You're coming with us↘  ← 끝을 내림 = 진술", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Asking whether the listener will come", "Apologizing for the change", "Treating it as already decided", "Offering the listener a choice"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "앞 문항과 단어는 완전히 같지만 끝을 내려 읽었다. 질문이 아니라 이미 정해진 일을 알리는 말이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0047", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0047.m4a", "transcript": "For the trip you'll need a hat, sunscreen, water...", "transcriptMarked": "a hat↗, sunscreen↗, water↗  ← 마지막 항목도 올림 = 목록 계속", "stem": "What does the intonation tell you?", "choices": ["Only three things are needed", "More items are still to come", "The speaker is unsure the trip will happen", "The listener already has these items"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "영어 목록에서 마지막 항목은 내림조로 끝나 완결을 알린다. 여기서는 'water'까지 올라가므로 아직 더 남았다는 신호다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0048", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0048.m4a", "transcript": "For the trip you'll need a hat, sunscreen, water.", "transcriptMarked": "a hat↗, sunscreen↗, water↘  ← 마지막만 내림 = 목록 끝", "stem": "What does the intonation tell you?", "choices": ["The list is complete", "The speaker forgot something", "More items will be added later", "The items are only suggestions"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "앞 문항과 항목은 같지만 마지막 'water'가 내림조다. 목록이 여기서 끝났다는 뜻이며, 이것이 영어 목록 억양의 기본 규칙이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0049", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0049.m4a", "transcript": "That was the right bus, wasn't it?", "transcriptMarked": "That was the right bus, wasn't it↗  ← 부가의문문을 올림 = 진짜 몰라서 묻는 것", "stem": "What does the speaker's intonation show?", "choices": ["He genuinely does not know and is worried", "He is certain and just wants agreement", "He is annoyed at the other person", "He is giving directions"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "부가의문문의 끝을 올리면 정말 확신이 없어 묻는 것이다. 내려 읽으면 '맞지?' 하고 동의를 구하는 것에 가깝다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0050", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0050.m4a", "transcript": "That was the right bus, wasn't it.", "transcriptMarked": "That was the right bus, wasn't it↘  ← 부가의문문을 내림 = 동의 구하기", "stem": "What does the speaker's intonation show?", "choices": ["He is not sure and needs an answer", "He thinks they took the wrong bus", "He is asking for directions", "He is fairly sure and expects agreement"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "같은 부가의문문이라도 내림조면 이미 확신이 있고 상대의 맞장구를 기대하는 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0051", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0051.m4a", "transcript": "She finished all of it?", "transcriptMarked": "She finished ALL of it↗↗  ← 높이 치솟는 올림조 = 놀람", "stem": "What is the speaker expressing?", "choices": ["Surprise that it was all done", "Disappointment at slow work", "A request for more work", "Doubt that the work was done well"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "평범한 확인 질문보다 훨씬 높이 올라가는 억양은 놀라움을 나타낸다. 예상보다 많이 했다는 뜻.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0052", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0052.m4a", "transcript": "He's already home.", "transcriptMarked": "He's already home↘  ← 평탄한 내림조 = 단순 진술", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Expressing disbelief", "Simply reporting a fact", "Asking where he is", "Warning the listener"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "끝이 담담하게 내려가면 감정이 실리지 않은 사실 전달이다. 놀랐다면 끝이 크게 올라갔을 것.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0053", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0053.m4a", "transcript": "Would you like some help?", "transcriptMarked": "Would you like some help↗  ← 부드러운 올림조 = 권유", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Insisting that the listener accept help", "Offering help in a friendly way", "Complaining about the listener's work", "Explaining how to do the task"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "올림조에 부드러운 어조가 얹히면 상대가 거절할 여지를 남기는 정중한 권유가 된다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0054", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0054.m4a", "transcript": "Could you say that again?", "transcriptMarked": "Could you say that again↗  ← 올림조 = 정중한 요청", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Politely asking for a repeat", "Correcting what was said", "Refusing to answer", "Agreeing with the speaker"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Could you ~?'를 올림조로 말하면 부탁이 된다. 내림조로 딱 잘라 말하면 지시에 가까워진다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0055", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0055.m4a", "transcript": "Do you want the red one, or the blue one?", "transcriptMarked": "the red one↗, or the blue one↘  ← 올렸다가 내림 = 둘 중 택일", "stem": "What kind of answer does the speaker expect?", "choices": ["Yes or no", "A choice between the two", "A reason for the choice", "No answer at all"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "선택의문문은 앞 항목을 올리고 마지막을 내린다. 둘 다 올리면 '뭐든 원하는 게 있나요?'라는 예/아니오 질문이 된다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0056", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0056.m4a", "transcript": "Do you want anything to drink?", "transcriptMarked": "anything to drink↗  ← 끝까지 올림 = 예/아니오 질문", "stem": "What kind of answer does the speaker expect?", "choices": ["A yes or no", "A choice among several drinks", "An explanation", "A promise"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "끝이 계속 올라가면 예/아니오를 묻는 것이다. 앞 문항처럼 올렸다 내렸다면 선택을 묻는 질문이 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0057", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0057.m4a", "transcript": "That's all for today.", "transcriptMarked": "That's all for today↘  ← 확실한 내림조 = 마무리", "stem": "What does the intonation signal?", "choices": ["One more thing is coming", "The speaker is asking a question", "The lesson is finished", "The speaker is unhappy"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "끝을 분명히 내리는 것은 '여기서 끝'이라는 신호다. 올렸다면 뭔가 더 이어질 것 같은 느낌을 준다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0058", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0058.m4a", "transcript": "First, we'll go over the notes...", "transcriptMarked": "go over the notes↗  ← 끝을 올린 채 멈춤 = 다음 단계 예고", "stem": "What does the intonation suggest?", "choices": ["This is the only step", "The plan has been canceled", "The notes are missing", "More steps will follow"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "'First'로 시작하고 끝을 올린 채 멈추면 뒤에 둘째·셋째가 이어진다는 신호다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0059", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0059.m4a", "transcript": "Girl: I left my project on the bus.\nBoy: You did what?", "transcriptMarked": "You did WHAT↗↗  ← 크게 치솟는 억양 = 충격", "stem": "Why does the boy speak that way?", "choices": ["He did not hear and wants a repeat", "He is bored by the story", "He is shocked by what she said", "He is correcting her grammar"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "되묻는 말을 아주 높은 올림조로 말하면 못 들어서가 아니라 믿기지 않아서 되묻는 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0060", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0060.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: They moved the deadline to next week.\nGirl: Really?", "transcriptMarked": "Really↗  ← 올림조 = 놀람 섞인 확인", "stem": "What does the girl mean?", "choices": ["She already knew about the change", "She thinks the boy is lying", "She is not interested", "She is surprised and wants confirmation"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "'Really'를 올려 말하면 '정말?' 하고 놀라며 확인하는 것이다. 내려 말하면 '그렇구나' 하는 담담한 반응이 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0061", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0061.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: They moved the deadline to next week.\nGirl: Really.", "transcriptMarked": "Really↘  ← 내림조 = 무덤덤한 반응", "stem": "What does the girl's tone show?", "choices": ["Excitement about the news", "A flat reaction without surprise", "Confusion about the date", "Anger at the change"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "같은 단어라도 내림조면 놀라움이 없다. 이미 알고 있었거나 별 관심이 없다는 뜻이다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0062", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0062.m4a", "transcript": "You're new here?", "transcriptMarked": "You're new here↗  ← 올림조 = 짐작한 것을 확인", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Telling the listener where to go", "Complaining about a newcomer", "Introducing herself", "Making a guess and checking it"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "평서문을 올림조로 말하면 '내 짐작이 맞나?' 하고 확인하는 것이다. 대화를 트는 흔한 방식이다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0063", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0063.m4a", "transcript": "Okay...", "transcriptMarked": "Okay...↗  ← 끌면서 끝을 흐림 = 미심쩍은 동의", "stem": "How does the speaker feel?", "choices": ["Not entirely convinced", "Fully convinced and ready", "Excited about the plan", "Angry about the decision"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "'Okay'를 끌면서 끝을 흐리면 완전한 동의가 아니다. 짧고 분명하게 내려 말했다면 확실한 수락이 된다.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0064", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0064.m4a", "transcript": "Anything else?", "transcriptMarked": "Anything else↗  ← 올림조 = 더 말해도 된다는 초대", "stem": "What is the speaker doing?", "choices": ["Ending the conversation firmly", "Refusing to answer more questions", "Repeating an earlier question", "Inviting the listener to add something"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "올림조로 물으면 상대에게 발언 기회를 열어 주는 것이다. 내려 말하면 '이제 그만'에 가깝게 들린다.", "difficulty": 2, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0065", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0065.m4a", "transcript": "Teacher: So you'd rather present on Friday.\nGirl: If that's okay?", "transcriptMarked": "If that's okay↗  ← 조건절만 남기고 올림 = 조심스러운 허락 요청", "stem": "What does the girl's intonation show?", "choices": ["She is asking permission, not stating a decision", "She has already made the change", "She disagrees with the teacher", "She did not understand the question"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "문장을 끝맺지 않고 조건절만 올림조로 남기면 결정을 상대에게 넘기는 정중한 표현이 된다.", "difficulty": 4, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3},
  {"id": "lis_0066", "track": "listening", "type": "mcq", "audio": "audio/lis_0066.m4a", "transcript": "Boy: Is there anything I should bring?\nTeacher: Just yourself.", "transcriptMarked": "Just yourself↘  ← 짧고 분명한 내림조 = 답 끝", "stem": "What does the teacher's intonation signal?", "choices": ["He is still thinking of other items", "He wants the student to ask again", "He is unhappy with the question", "That is the complete answer"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "짧게 내려 끝맺으면 더 보탤 말이 없다는 뜻이다. 끝을 올렸다면 뭔가 더 떠올리는 중처럼 들렸을 것.", "difficulty": 3, "tags": ["listening", "prosody", "intonation"], "replayLimit": 3}
]);
